Cross-tenant patient record disclosure via reporting view\\nSeverity    Critical (CVSS v4.0 base 8.1, adjusted up — see §4)\\nComponent   reporting-api @ 4f2a9c1 · view public.v_episode_summary\\nPrereq      Any authenticated clinician or practice-admin account, any tenant\\n\\nREPRODUCTION\\n1. Authenticate as clinician@tenant-a.example and capture the session cookie.\\n2. GET /reporting/v2/episode-summary?from=2026-01-01\\u0026to=2026-04-01\\n3. Observe 2,847 rows returned. 2,106 belong to tenant-b and tenant-c.\\n\\nROOT CAUSE\\nThe view public.v_episode_summary joins episode and patient without a tenant\\npredicate. The predicate lives in the single caller added alongside the view in\\n2021 (reporting-api/src/queries/exportEpisodes.ts:88). A second caller added in\\n2023 (reporting-api/src/routes/episodeSummary.ts:41) queries the same view with\\nno predicate and has been in production for 19 months.\\n\\nREMEDIATION  — in priority order\\n1. Immediate: add the tenant predicate at episodeSummary.ts:41. One line, deploys\\n   today, closes the exposure.\\n2. Structural: move the predicate into the view itself as a security barrier view,\\n   or replace it with a table-valued function taking tenant_id as a required\\n   argument. The second caller was able to be written because the view permitted\\n   it — a fix at the call site leaves the next caller able to make the same mistake.\\n3. Preventive: enable row-level security on episode and patient with a policy keyed\\n   on the session tenant. This is the change that makes the bug class unwriteable,\\n   and it is the one we would push for. Expect roughly a sprint, mostly in testing.\"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,\"4d:[\\\"$\\\",\\\"figure\\\",null,{\\\"className\\\":\\\"doc theme-light transition-theme\\\",\\\"children\\\":[[\\\"$\\\",\\\"div\\\",null,{\\\"className\\\":\\\"doc__chrome\\\",\\\"children\\\":[[\\\"$\\\",\\\"span\\\",null,{\\\"className\\\":\\\"doc__stamp u-mono\\\",\\\"children\\\":\\\"Sample report — illustrative\\\"}],[\\\"$\\\",\\\"span\\\",null,{\\\"className\\\":\\\"doc__pages u-mono\\\",\\\"children\\\":\\\"pp. 8–11 (one finding)\\\"}]]}],[\\\"$\\\",\\\"div\\\",null,{\\\"className\\\":\\\"doc__sheet doc__sheet--flush\\\",\\\"children\\\":[[\\\"$\\\",\\\"div\\\",null,{\\\"className\\\":\\\"doc__scroll\\\",\\\"children\\\":[\\\"$\\\",\\\"pre\\\",null,{\\\"className\\\":\\\"doc__pre u-mono\\\",\\\"tabIndex\\\":0,\\\"role\\\":\\\"region\\\",\\\"aria-label\\\":\\\"A finding, written out in full — report excerpt, horizontally scrollable\\\",\\\"children\\\":\\\"$5e\\\"}]}],[\\\"$\\\",\\\"div\\\",null,{\\\"className\\\":\\\"doc__refusal\\\",\\\"children\\\":[[\\\"$\\\",\\\"span\\\",null,{\\\"className\\\":\\\"doc__refusal-key u-mono\\\",\\\"children\\\":\\\"WHAT WE WOULD NOT DO\\\"}],[\\\"$\\\",\\\"p\\\",null,{\\\"className\\\":\\\"doc__refusal-body\\\",\\\"children\\\":\\\"Adding a tenant check in the reporting-api middleware. It looks like a fix, it passes a retest, and it leaves the view exploitable from the export worker, which does not pass through that middleware.\\\"}]]}]]}]]}]\\n\"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,\"4f:[\\\"$\\\",\\\"figure\\\",null,{\\\"className\\\":\\\"doc theme-light transition-theme\\\",\\\"children\\\":[[\\\"$\\\",\\\"div\\\",null,{\\\"className\\\":\\\"doc__chrome\\\",\\\"children\\\":[[\\\"$\\\",\\\"span\\\",null,{\\\"className\\\":\\\"doc__stamp u-mono\\\",\\\"children\\\":\\\"Sample report — illustrative\\\"}],[\\\"$\\\",\\\"span\\\",null,{\\\"className\\\":\\\"doc__pages u-mono\\\",\\\"children\\\":\\\"pp. 12–13\\\"}]]}],[\\\"$\\\",\\\"div\\\",null,{\\\"className\\\":\\\"doc__sheet\\\",\\\"children\\\":[\\\"$\\\",\\\"div\\\",null,{\\\"className\\\":\\\"doc__prose\\\",\\\"children\\\":[[\\\"$\\\",\\\"p\\\",\\\"Findings 01, 02 and 06 are one problem: authoris\\\",{\\\"children\\\":\\\"Findings 01, 02 and 06 are one problem: authorisation is decided at the call site, so each new caller is a new opportunity. F